$DIR/test.p:3:32: mixture of field:value and value elements in struct literal
    A struct literal either names every field it sets (Point{X: 1, Y: 2}) or
    lists a value for every field in order (Point{1, 2}). It cannot mix the two.
    (see "Composite literals" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.3)
    (run "pluto explain E0064" for a longer explanation)
